{
  "name": "local-llm",
  "about": "Run open-weight LLMs on this workspace's GPU (llama.cpp, ik_llama.cpp, Ollama, vLLM, TabbyAPI; LM Studio for internal use only); weights download only on Run",
  "description": "Runs open-source LLMs on this machine's GPU with llama.cpp, ik_llama.cpp or Ollama, and with vLLM or TabbyAPI once an admin installs them. LM Studio is proprietary and for internal use only: it stays off unless the deployment's operator sets ploinky var LOCAL_LLM_LMSTUDIO internal-use and restarts local-llm, and an admin must then accept its Terms to install it. Admins pick a model and a runner in Settings; weights download only when Run is pressed. Its manifest declares GPU access (containerSecurity.gpu); on the host, ploinky gpu revoke --agent local-llms/local-llm takes it away and ploinky gpu grant --agent local-llms/local-llm restores it.",
  "container": "docker.io/assistos/local-llm@sha256:b6c79af2aad08b542339346f4a985c84d5cbcacc31e8c6df45f951da7ba0fbf7",
  "agent": "exec node /code/src/main.mjs",
  "readiness": {
    "protocol": "mcp"
  },
  "volumes": {
    ".data/local-llm": "/data"
  },
  "containerSecurity": {
    "gpu": true,
    "shmSize": "8g"
  },
  "routerAccess": {
    "agentPorts": false
  },
  "ideSettings": [
    {
      "key": "local-llm-settings",
      "label": "Local LLMs",
      "scope": "workspace",
      "pluginKey": "local-llm/local-llm-settings",
      "settingsComponent": "local-llm-settings",
      "adminOnly": true
    }
  ],
  "endpoints": {
    "chatCompletions": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": [
        "/code/src/chatResponder.mjs"
      ],
      "cwd": "/code",
      "timeoutMs": 600000,
      "supportsStream": true
    }
  },
  "capabilities": {
    "tags": [
      "local-llm"
    ],
    "summary": "Serves the open-weight model an administrator runs on this workspace's GPU.",
    "whenToUse": "Call soul_gateway/local-llms/local-llm/default for private, on-machine generation once a model is ready; it answers 503 not_ready otherwise."
  },
  "profiles": {
    "default": {
      "env": {
        "HF_TOKEN": {
          "required": false
        },
        "LOCAL_LLM_LMSTUDIO": {
          "required": false
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
{
  "name": "local-llm",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "test": "node --test tests/*.test.mjs"
  }
}
# local-llm Specification Matrix

The `local-llm` agent keeps its own specification set. Its numbering is local to this directory and is separate from the repository-level sequence under `docs/specs/`, which describes the legacy shared-image agents.

| Spec | Title | Status | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [DS000](DS000-vision-and-scope.md) | Vision and Scope | accepted | What local-llm is, how it differs from the legacy agents, its runners (LM Studio for internal use only), and what it deliberately leaves out. |
| [DS001](DS001-agent-contract.md) | Agent Contract | accepted | Manifest, process model, tools, authorization, the chat endpoint, drain, and LM Studio's operator switch and limits. |
| [DS002](DS002-model-lifecycle.md) | Model Lifecycle | accepted | Catalog, registry, on-demand download, the deployment state machine, and restart behaviour. Records what is reused from repository DS008. |
| [DS003](DS003-gpu-and-resources.md) | GPU and Resources | accepted | The Box GPU grant, admission, runner isolation, and memory estimates. Records what is reused from repository DS010. |
| [DS004](DS004-on-demand-runners.md) | On-demand Runners | accepted | Runners installed after the image is built: the lock in the image, the verified cache in /data, the runnable copy rebuilt in the container, and the CI install check, which never downloads a proprietary entry. |

Tests, from the repository root: `node --test 'local-llm/tests/*.test.mjs'` or `npm --prefix local-llm test` (no Docker, GPU or network required). A bare directory argument does not work on Node 24.

